      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Figure 1: Example of a BPMN 2.0 process model showing a 'Restaurant' pool with three lanes (Customer: Hungry -> Order Burger -> AND split / XOR loop with 10 min Timer Event 'No Burger Received' -> 'Poke the Waiter' vs 'Burger Received' -> Receive the Burger -> Eat the Burger -> Full; Waiter: Take the Order -> Serve the Burger; Chef: Subprocess 'Make the Burger'), annotated with red callout labels naming core BPMN 2.0 constructs (Pool, Lane, Start Event, AND Gateway, XOR Gateway, Timer Event, Activity, Subprocess, Sequence Flow, End Event).",
          "lang": "en",
